   <p><note place="header">158</note></p>
<p><date when="1861">1861</date> Executive Journal</p>
<p><date when="1861-01-11">Jany 11</date>. 
<lb/>The <persName ref="cwgk:N00000258">Governor</persName> approved the following accounts to the City of <placeName ref="cwgk:P00000308">Frankfort</placeName> for gas for the month of January</p>
<p><table rend="rules">
<row>
	<cell>Governors' House</cell>
	<cell>$5.40</cell>
</row>
<row>
	<cell><persName ref="cwgk:N00000466">Auditor</persName>s &amp; <persName ref="cwgk:N00001049">Treasurer</persName>s Office</cell>
	<cell>31.95</cell>
</row>
<row>
	<cell>Governors &amp; <persName ref="cwgk:N00002581">Secretary</persName>s "</cell>
	<cell>8.55</cell>
</row>
</table></p>
<p>Also an account of $1.00. to <persName ref="cwgk:N00017483">James Penn</persName> for packing public books in <orgName ref="cwgk:O00010811">State Arsenal</orgName></p>
<p>Also account of $4.<hi rend="underline">60</hi> to <persName ref="cwgk:N00021519">Frank Nolls</persName> for painting and glazing done in State Capitol.</p>
<p>And account of $6.<hi rend="underline">90</hi> to <persName ref="cwgk:N00021520">Nancy Morton</persName> for washing &amp;<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">c</hi></hi> done at Auditors' office, certified as correct by the <persName ref="cwgk:N00002894">Assistant Auditor</persName>.</p>
<p>He commissioned <persName ref="cwgk:N00004530">Jno. L. Phythian</persName> Assistant Surgeon in <orgName ref="cwgk:O00000303">Ky State Guard</orgName></p>
<p>And <persName ref="cwgk:N00021521">Tho. G. Calvert</persName> 2<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">d</hi></hi> Lieutenant in the State Guard</p>
<p>Also <persName ref="cwgk:N00021522">R. W. Woolley</persName> 1<hi rend="underline"><hi rend="sup">st</hi></hi> Lieutenant in the <orgName ref="cwgk:O00000916">Lexington Rifles</orgName>, duly elected.</p>
